  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`PendingAssessment` (src/authoring/mod.rs:171-177) is a data carrier holding the subject, the evidence record (a generic `serde_json::Value`), the outcome and the usage log. It does not write files, choose the destination, fix the evidence schema or set validation status. Those jobs belong to `AuthoringSubject::evidence_path`, `write_record` (batch.rs) and `PendingAssessment::persisted`, which carry their own `{impl}` references to `requirements.authoring.persistence`. The struct is not a test, so `{test}` does not apply, and it implements no part of the requirement, so `{impl}` does not apply either. Its fields follow the persistence requirement: the subject gives the evidence path and the record is what gets written. A change to that text could therefore require changing the struct, so `{cite}` is the correct role. It has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same requirement, so the citation is not redundant.",
  "inputs": [
